  "term": "meprobamate",
  "definition": "Meprobamate is a carbamate drug with sedative, sleep-inducing, and some muscle-relaxing effects. In mental health care, it has been used to treat anxiety disorders and for short-term management of insomnia, though it has largely been replaced by benzodiazepines.",
